    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12701" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēflā^grātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		deflagro, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a burning up, consuming by fire, conflagration</i>
			(perhaps only in Cic.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">futura aliquando caeli atque terrarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. 1, 49, 111</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terrarum omnium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fin. 3, 19 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>destruction</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Planc. 40, 95</span></i></div>
